 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
-- Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
+- Only managers may freeze a project (`POST /projects/{pid}/freeze`). Freezing sets every member's role to `viewer`, managers included, and returns the members sorted by user ID. A frozen project rejects all task writes with 403, since no one is a contributor or manager any more. Reads still work. There is no unfreeze endpoint, and a frozen project cannot be frozen again.
+- Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work), including freeze.
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
